From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: don't wake the system on charger updates

The ADSP charger firmware sends BATTMGR_NOTIFICATION on every battery or
USB change, many per minute while charging. Each one calls
power_supply_changed(), whose pm_stay_awake() is a wakeup event: with the
IPCC mailbox IRQ left unmasked in suspend (as it is upstream), s2idle
resumes in full within minutes.

Register the power supplies without a wakeup source, so the notifications
are handled in suspend without waking the system. Masking the IPCC IRQ
across suspend instead (the old 20-sm8550/0502) keeps the AP asleep but
leaves the firmware's messages unanswered: about five minutes into s2idle
the charger stops drawing power, and a device asleep on its charger runs
the battery flat.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1656,6 +1656,15 @@
 	psy_cfg_supply.supplied_to = qcom_battmgr_battery;
 	psy_cfg_supply.num_supplicants = 1;
 
+	/*
+	 * The charger firmware sends a notification on every change, and
+	 * power_supply_changed() reports each one as a wakeup event, which
+	 * aborts suspend-to-idle within minutes. Those updates aren't a reason
+	 * to wake the system.
+	 */
+	psy_cfg.no_wakeup_source = true;
+	psy_cfg_supply.no_wakeup_source = true;
+
 	mutex_init(&battmgr->lock);
 	init_completion(&battmgr->ack);
 
